{"kind":"artifact","text":"notes/2026-10-01-jam-room.md at exact 5eb8c84f643c0121e0b11f12929c98428e1a3c1a on request/jam-room-note, under promise 18c400e0 on request f4a626c8\n\nThe jam-room design note: several agent musicians and one human improvise in an Artroom room as a freeform, non-GitHub demonstration. It covers the timing model (a committed change takes effect at the first bar boundary at least one lookahead after its admission time `at`), what lives in room acts, repository files and a live layer that is never authoritative, the sample library with a provenance-checking sample checker, the agent harness (symbolic perception, phrase and bandmate loops, long-lived agents), the human with MIDI and a stage client, the four moments where the room is visible, landing load, the places that press on the zero-contract-amendment criterion, risks including the contest's original-work rule, and two spikes (J1 timing on the deployed room, J2 agents trading fours) with frozen claims and stop rules. Measured figures are cited from the room-core and sandbox-git spikes; everything else is labelled unmeasured. Documentation only.","body":{"commit":"5eb8c84f643c0121e0b11f12929c98428e1a3c1a","path":"notes/2026-10-01-jam-room.md"}}